WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
Welcome to Grade 2 English, Unit 6: All About Bugs.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:09.120
In this unit you explore the tiny world of
bugs, insects and other small garden animals.

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.380
You learn the names of the butterfly,
cricket, ant, bee, spider and worm,

4
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:19.140
and you find out what makes an animal an insect:
six legs, three body parts and two antennae.

5
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:26.100
You learn position words such as on, under, between and
above so that you can say exactly where a creature is,

6
00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.500
and you use the simple present tense to give true facts.

7
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.660
By the end you can describe a creature of
your own, just like Amal in this unit's story,

8
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.940
“Amal and the Little Garden Friends”.

9
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.780
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:50.380
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
bugs and garden animals: butterfly, cricket, ant, bee,

11
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.420
spider and worm.

12
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:58.780
You will also say what makes an animal an insect:
six legs, three body parts and two antennae.

13
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.460
You will also explain why a spider and a worm are not insects.

14
00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.060
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:11.080
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: turn, burn, hurt, shirt, pretty, rock.

16
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.700
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

17
00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:20.640
The reading sequence includes What Is an Insect?

18
00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.060
and A Bug Poem.

19
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.220
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

20
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.080
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

21
00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.900
The first language focus is Position Words.

22
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.700
Position words tell us where something is.

23
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:47.400
When we watch bugs we need them to say exactly where each
creature sits: on a leaf, under a rock, or inside a hole.

24
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.560
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

25
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.840
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Name and Describe a Bug.

26
00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.920
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

27
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.480
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

28
00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.320
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.500
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

30
00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:20.800
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
